# Why EuroZig when there is already ZSF?

EuroZig is focused on nurturing a growing Zig ecosystem within the EU
by leveraging opportunities exclusively available to European non-profit
organizations (e.g. EU-only grants).

Additionally, as a German non-profit organization, EuroZig can act as
the fiscal host for initiatives across europe such as conferences, workshops
and [Zig Day](https://zig.day) events.

At the moment of writing, EuroZig is planned to become the fiscal host for
[Zigtoberfest](https://zigtoberfest.de) starting from 2027.

# What is EuroZig's relationship to ZSF?

EuroZig is not directly affiliated with [Zig Software
Foundation](https://ziglang.org/zsf/), meaning that donating to one
organization **will not** make the funds available to the other.

Both organizations share a compatible mission, albeit EuroZig focuses its
efforts on the European Union.

Most notably, **funds donated to ZSF will directly go towards paying core team
members to work on Zig, while donations to EuroZig will go towards growing the
Zig community within the EU**, mainly though social events and workshops.

# Can my donations to EuroZig be tax-deductible?

Tax-deducibility of donations can have complex interactions depending on your fiscal status.
We invite you to double check with an accredited accountant or comparable professional to
know precisely whether you can deduct donations to non-profit organizations.

That said, as a broad, non-authoritative answer:

- **German taxpayers** who donate directly to EuroZig should be able to deduct their donations.
- **European taxpayers** who donate via [Giving Europe](https://giving.eu) should be able to deduct their donations.
- **Non-European taxpayers** should generally **not expect** to be able to deduct their donations.

